# Exact arithmetic. Every number here is exact unless it is asked to be a
# Num, a floating-point number, as the Float column is.

sheet Sums

Case            | Exact                 | Float                           | Same
Tenths          | = 0.1 + 0.2           | = 0.1.Num + 0.2.Num             | *
Take away       | = 1 - 0.9             | = 1.Num - 0.9.Num               | *
Squared         | = 1.1 * 1.1           | = 1.1.Num * 1.1.Num             | *
Big numbers     | = 2**64 + 1 - 2**64   | = 2.Num**64 + 1 - 2.Num**64     | *
Ten years at 5% | = 1000 * (1 + 5%)**10 | = 1000.Num * (1 + 0.05.Num)**10 | *

Same := Exact == Float

sheet Split

# A bill split three ways stays exact: the shares add back to the bill.

Person | Share
Ana    | *
Ben    | *
Cy     | *

Share := 100 / 3

sheet Check

Item             | Value
Bill             | 100
Shares added up  | = Split.Share.sum()
Nothing lost     | = Split.Share.sum() == 100
